{"kind":"finding","id":"FN-B-run-phone-tracker-components-2-b-01","date":"2026-11-25","lens":"gap-8","surface":"phone","area":"phone/tracker-components-2","refs":["F-phone-810","FN-L14-phone-tracker-components-2-01"],"severity":"S3","title":"A Hevy link import can add every unknown exercise as new without asking","what":"When a member brings routines in from a Hevy share link, the app first checks which exercises it does not have yet and shows them, each with a 'same as' suggestion, so the member can match or leave them out. If that check cannot read the phone's exercise list, the failure is swallowed: the step is skipped with no word and no log line, and Save then adds every unknown exercise as a brand-new custom exercise. If only the suggestions fail, the list shows with no 'same as' offers and no word why.","expected":"If the check of new exercises fails, the member is told and can try again, and the error is logged; exercises are never created without the member having seen the list.","evidence":["apps/mobile/src/tracker/components/RoutineImportSteps.tsx:281-289","apps/mobile/src/tracker/services/routineImport.ts:265-275","apps/mobile/src/tracker/services/routineImport.ts:191-199"],"proof":"code-read","root_cause_key":"new-exercise-check-failure-swallowed","who":"members","how_often":"only when the phone's exercise list cannot be read","fix_line":"On a failed check, show a try-again message and log it instead of skipping the step","fix_size":"small","needs_him":false,"verified":"pending","status":"open"}
